    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0222" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/4353</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4686</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-04">October 4, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        9.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    concerning Central Tinguaro, especially my despatch No. 4582 of September 24,
                        1943<anchor n="18" xml:id="d193-f1"/> transmitting a copy of my note to the
                    Foreign Office<anchor n="19" xml:id="d193-f2"/> in the premises, I have the
                    honor to enclose copy and translation of the reply,<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d193-f3"/> which I have received from the Minister of State.</p>
                <p>This reply is merely an acknowledgment stating that the “matter is the subject of
                    the preferential attention of the pertinent authorities…”<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d193-f4"/>
                    <pb facs="0223" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/> and that “it will be a pleasure” to
                    inform me in due course of their decision.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spruille Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
